# Paragraph ▸ Alert quotes the paragraph as that alert, switches an alert's
# kind, and takes the quote away when its own kind is chosen again. The
# caret keeps its place in the text.
write @DIR@/doc.md Text here.\n
cmd openPath @DIR@/doc.md
wait 400
caret 0 4
cmd alert TIP
wait 300
check view.itemAt(0).alert === "tip"
cmd alert WARNING
wait 300
check view.itemAt(0).alert === "warning"
cmd alert WARNING
wait 300
check view.itemAt(0).alert === ""
type  more
dump @OUT@
